WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.535
Britt: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.437
we wanted to find out the differences

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.172
between Hungry Jack's Australia

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.041
and Burger King in the US.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.043
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.780
First things first.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.182
You might have noticed there's
a difference in the name.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.217
Here in Australia,

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:20.220
Burger King operates under
the name Hungry Jack's

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.855
because when they first came here,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.356
their name was already taken.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.991
We'll get more into the history later,

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.961
but when you hear me saying
Hungry Jack's, that's why.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.729
Now let's get into the drinks.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.065
In Australia, our Hungry Jack's drinks

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:36.569
come in three sizes,
small, medium, and large.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:40.006
In the US, our Burger King
drinks come in four sizes.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.209
The value, the small,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.812
the medium, and the large.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.447
Let's measure them to keep them honest.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.549
To be fair to Burger
King, I filled these up.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.151
I think I did a pretty good job.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.886
The lid's a little recessed.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.087
Yes, there's ice in there.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:57.023
Britt: Now let's measure the large.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.329
Joe: I feel like everything
is about 4 or 5 ounces off.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.000
Our fries, or chips, as we
like to call them in Australia,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.404
come in three sizes,
small, medium, and large.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.139
Our fries come in four sizes.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:17.677
The little value, the small,
the medium, and the large.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.245
And you know we're gonna weigh 'em.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.815
So, these portions should weigh 90 grams,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.251
116 grams, and 166 grams,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.420
according to the Hungry Jack's website.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.957
So let's see if this is true.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.392
That's convenient.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:39.065
Both Australia and the
US have the Whopper,

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:42.535
so let's weigh both of them and compare.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.369
All right.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.574
On to the nuggets.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:51.478
In Australia, our nuggets
come in four sizes,

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.546
three, six,

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.715
12, and 18.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.885
Our US nuggets come
technically in three sizes,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.554
the four-piece; the eight-piece,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.789
which, in some parts of the country

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.792
you can also get the fiery
nugget version in eight-piece;

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.361
and a 16-piece, which was not available.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.532
Well, I want to be in the shot.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.566
I'm just kidding.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.401
Because this is my new headshot.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.637
Here in the US, we have
four sizes of onion rings.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.773
Again, value, small, medium, and large.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:24.444
In Australia, our onion
rings come in two sizes,

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.479
a medium and a large.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.881
Just eyeballing it right now,

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:31.284
looks like we have bigger
portion sizes than Australia.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.086
I'm going to count out
the rings in the largest

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.721
and see how it compares to theirs.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:38.191
Britt: So, in a large serving,
we get 12 onion rings.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.493
OK, so this, this is one
of the smaller ones we had.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.664
Here is everything that you'll find

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.366
at an Australian Hungry Jack's

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.302
that you won't find in
an American Burger King.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.603
And here's everything you can get

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.606
at a Burger King/Hungry Jack's in America

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.208
that you can't get in Australia.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.077
Let's get into the burgers.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.748
I have to say, my
observation in all of this

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.918
is all of these burgers,
not only are they massive,

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.986
but they look really good.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.355
We have a Whiskey River Whopper.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.024
You've got onion, you've got lettuce,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:14.460
you have chips inside, you have tomatoes.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.396
Two layers of cheese,

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.498
two burger patties.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.537
I really like this. I
really, really like this.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:27.207
The burgers are better at Hungry Jack's!

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.242
So, there's a saying in Australia,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.644
it's one of their slogans,
and they always say,

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.546
"The burgers are better at Hungry Jack's."

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.782
And this is really good.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.884
I can't taste whiskey specifically.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.753
I don't know if it's ...
I'm not drunk yet.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.023
So I think there's not whiskey in there,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.060
but I think it must be,
like, a whiskey glaze

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.661
or a whiskey sauce.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.464
It's like a caramelized flavor.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.767
We have these exclusive US burgers,

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.570
starting all the way down there.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.974
A Texas double Whopper. Same
as a regular double Whopper,

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:04.310
but this one has jalapeños.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.878
Tejas.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.247
OK, so you're getting your money's worth.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:10.350
Oh, there's also bacon
in there too? All right.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.584
Pretty good. I don't know
if I could eat a whole one

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.585
of those, but I like that.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.922
We have a double Whiskey River Whopper,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.791
an ultimate double Whopper,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.961
which is two layers of beef
and two layers of cheese.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.330
We have your classic Whopper,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.466
a double Whopper and cheese,

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.568
a triple Whopper and cheese,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:31.471
and an Angry Whopper.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.207
And it comes with a single
patty or a double patty,

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.410
or there's a triple-beef
option if that's what you like.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.713
And with angry onions.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.449
I don't know what an angry onion is.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.319
I've never met an angry onion before.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:50.490
All right, let's have a
bite of the Angry Whopper.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.461
There's a bit of a spice to it.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.597
Nothing too overpowering.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.899
It's quite nice. I like this as well.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.801
But that's really, like,
a nice subtle kick to it.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.370
So that's what makes it
angry, if you were wondering.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.472
I'm so happy I could solve
that problem for you,

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.041
because I'm here to serve.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.642
If double meat isn't enough for you,

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.879
we also have the triple
Whopper, Australia.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:17.050
Yes, you are correct. That is a bun,

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:22.955
then a piece of meat, and
then another piece of meat,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.624
and then a third piece of meat,

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:25.858
and then all the stuff.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.129
You just jump in the middle of the meat.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.664
You can't just go meat, meat, meat.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.232
Our Whopper doesn't
automatically have cheese.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.401
You can get a Whopper
with cheese, obviously.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.203
So this one doesn't have cheese.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.538
Texas did have cheese.

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:42.342
I don't know why cheese isn't
the default for the Whopper.

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:44.310
The Whopper has been around for so long,

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.312
back when people wanted regular hamburgers

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.681
and not cheeseburgers, which
I think is just insanity.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.351
And then we have the bacon deluxe.

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:54.287
This is very similar to the
ultimate double Whopper.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:58.024
The sizing is the main
difference that I can tell,

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.159
and obviously with the patties and stuff,

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.129
but the flavor is supposed to be the same.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:07.767
We also have the barbecue
bacon Whopper Jr.,

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.103
which of course has bacon, American bacon.

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:11.237
Now's the perfect time.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:14.540
I know that she was talking
about close-up of the bacon,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.508
so why don't I just do a little

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.310
something right here for her?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.712
All right. All right,
check it out, Australia.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.114
American bacon.

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.982
We got the strip bacon.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.617
Let's get a good glamour
shot. Now we're big.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.153
Look at the strips! We got the strips.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:30.623
So, the bacon in Hungry Jack's
is Australian eye bacon,

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:34.727
and it looks something like this,

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.797
if you can manage to see
it past all this sauce.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.900
I know you guys in
America generally prefer

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.503
your bacon to be a bit
crispier and thinner.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.438
We do have that option here.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.140
However, our rashers of bacon

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.909
do tend to be quite a thicker portion.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:53.079
So it is thin and crispy on the outside,

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.481
but the inside, see how it's, like, a,

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.417
it's a nice bit of pork?

00:06:57.417 --> 00:07:00.353
Speaking of bacon, we have the bacon king.

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:02.855
It feels like it's just the
Whopper without the vegetables,

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.023
which I applaud.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.592
Look, everyone, they put
cheese in between the meat.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.327
See? They know how to
do it. This is great.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.729
I don't know why this has
to be a whole different

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.597
menu thing. Just call this the —

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:12.832
this should be the Whopper.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.835
And then we have a Whopper Jr. and cheese,

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.670
little baby Whopper,

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.605
and then a triple cheeseburger

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.941
and a barbecue cheeseburger.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.709
Moving on to the much smaller burgers.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.012
Look at this, man. These
are tiny little guys.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:27.013
Bacon cheeseburger.

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.214
If you want a little
more meat in your mouth,

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.048
and you know I do,

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:31.517
go ahead and get yourself the double.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:35.621
Yo, Australia!

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:36.856
Look at that cheese pull.

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.724
It's like an Insider video
from three years ago.

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:40.393
I have no idea what rodeo,

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:44.230
if rodeos exist outside of
the States or the Americas.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.999
And if they don't, we have
a thing called rodeos.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:49.135
And for some reason we
have a Rodeo Burger,

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:51.103
and that's just a cheeseburger

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:53.272
with barbecue sauce and onion rings.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:56.342
And now we have our
Grill Master collection.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.578
So, this is made from

00:07:58.578 --> 00:08:01.614
thick, juicy Angus.

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:02.915
Starting off to my right,

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:06.419
we have the Grill Masters
pulled pork and Angus.

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:09.555
They went hard on the pulled pork.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.591
They didn't shy away from that.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.095
You can taste the barbecue sauce,

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.697
which is surprising because it didn't look

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:20.099
like there was much barbecue sauce on it.

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:22.802
The pork flavor's coming
through ever so slightly.

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.770
But it's just the texture
of the pulled pork

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.341
and a solid beef patty that

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.009
I don't really like that much.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:33.813
We have our Grill Master cowboy Angus.

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:37.950
We have our Grill Master
double cowboy Angus,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.785
with two Angus patties.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:44.390
And then we have our Grill
Masters Chicago Angus patty.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:49.262
Double bacon, natural
cheese, and peppercorn sauce.

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:50.429
I'm also curious to know, like,

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.131
why do they make a Chicago burger?

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:54.166
What is a Chicago burger?

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.701
Is Chicago a peppery city?

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:56.836
I thought it was the Windy City.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:09:00.540
It has a patty, it's got some
lettuce, iceberg lettuce,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.010
a sauce, which I presume
has pepper in it, obviously,

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.546
otherwise, don't know what
that black stuff is in it.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.447
That would be questionable.

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:13.419
And it has a layer of cheese
and bacon and tomatoes.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:16.722
I think maybe the reason
it's a Chicago-style burger

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.257
is because of the double bacon.

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:21.027
I know in the early part of last century

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:24.196
the stockyards were
really popular in Chicago.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:26.966
Upton Sinclair wrote a book
about it called "The Jungle."

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:28.734
Don't read it. It's a real bummer.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.505
This is — I prefer this to that.

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:34.840
This has a lot more flavor.
The textures are good.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.811
I like the combination of
the bacon and the Angus beef.

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:39.946
It's really messy, though,

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:41.581
so don't take someone out on a first date

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.349
and get the Chicago burger.

00:09:43.349 --> 00:09:47.453
And now we have our Grill
Masters Angus, bacon, and cheese

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:51.891
and then the Grill Masters
double Angus, bacon, and cheese.

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:56.662
So there's two Angus patties
and two layers of cheese.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:10:00.199
I just have to say I'm really
impressed by Hungry Jack's.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:03.469
I find that their burgers
are really, really good,

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:05.504
and the quality is unreal.

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:06.639
Here are all the chicken options

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:08.307
exclusive over here in the US.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:11.777
Down here, we have the
BK royal crispy chicken.

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:13.112
Royal.

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:15.481
The Burger King royal, the BK royal.

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.517
Fit for King ...

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:22.388
Philip? Charles.

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:24.156
Australia, I don't know if
you're aware of this, but there's

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:27.727
a chicken-sandwich civil war
going on in this country.

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:31.063
Every single fast-food place
has their chicken sandwich.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:34.400
I think Chick-fil-A just
came in, got everyone scared.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.968
Every fast-food place, every burger place

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:38.971
has at least four chicken
sandwiches, sometimes more.

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.173
And Burger King, I gotta
say they did a good job.

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:42.742
Been sitting for a minute, still crispy.

00:10:42.742 --> 00:10:45.011
Very impressive. Crispy's in the title.

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:46.312
Here are all the chicken options

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.180
that you can get at Hungry Jack's.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.783
The Whiskey River Jack's fried chicken.

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:55.521
So, you have some lettuce,
you have your whiskey sauce

00:10:55.521 --> 00:11:00.259
with some chips, onion ring maybe?

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:04.196
The spicy BK royal crispy chicken sando.

00:11:04.196 --> 00:11:05.598
Generous with the mayo.

00:11:05.598 --> 00:11:08.567
They're moving mayo at
BK. They're moving mayo.

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:10.736
Everything is chicken
with mayo. I don't mind.

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:14.774
It's got more heat than
I thought it would.

00:11:16.075 --> 00:11:17.710
Nothing I can't handle, but yeah.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.613
The Whiskey River grilled chicken,

00:11:20.613 --> 00:11:23.182
the classic Jack's fried chicken.

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:25.885
This is just fried chicken
with some mayonnaise

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:28.054
and some iceberg lettuce.

00:11:28.054 --> 00:11:31.257
This spicy Jack's fried chicken,

00:11:31.257 --> 00:11:34.727
and it has spicy sauce on that.

00:11:34.727 --> 00:11:37.763
Australia, we also have a bacon and Swiss

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:41.934
BK royal crispy chicken
sandwich, and here it is.

00:11:44.437 --> 00:11:46.038
That's good. It's a good
combo. That's really good.

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:46.872
I like that.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:48.240
I probably would get that
one over all the other ones.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.445
The cheesy bacon classic
Jack's fried chicken,

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:55.881
the cheesy bacon spicy
Jack's fried chicken.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:58.050
So, this would be the spicy sauce.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.019
That's a lot of spicy sauce.

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:04.356
The spicy grilled chicken,
the grilled chicken,

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:07.560
the grilled chicken with bacon and cheese.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.662
And of course this little
guy, the chicken Jr.

00:12:09.662 --> 00:12:12.898
If you've ever had a McChicken,
it's the same exact thing.

00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:14.533
Whoa, what's going on here?

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:16.035
Is that sauce, or is that, like ... ?

00:12:16.035 --> 00:12:19.105
Started skimping on —
no, because mayo's on top.

00:12:19.105 --> 00:12:20.706
So what's that?

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:22.975
I'm not licking it!

00:12:26.412 --> 00:12:28.781
Maybe it is mayo. I don't know what it is.

00:12:28.781 --> 00:12:33.686
I want to try the cheesy bacon
spicy Jack's fried chicken

00:12:33.686 --> 00:12:37.957
because I haven't been
able to get a spicy burger,

00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:40.025
and this looks like it is

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:45.064
packed with spice.

00:12:45.064 --> 00:12:48.334
So let's take a bite into it and see

00:12:48.334 --> 00:12:49.635
how spicy it really is.

00:12:51.337 --> 00:12:55.241
That is very spicy.
Definitely recommend this one.

00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:56.976
This one's really, really good.

00:12:56.976 --> 00:12:57.810
It's such a relief,

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.012
because I feel like every
burger that we've had is, like,

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:03.616
says it's spicy, but it's like, where?

00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:05.017
And last but not least,

00:13:05.017 --> 00:13:07.653
we have some additional exclusive items!

00:13:07.653 --> 00:13:09.789
At the Burger King, we have a big fish,

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:11.690
which is our fish sandwich.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:15.194
Rivals, of course the Filet-O-Fish.

00:13:15.194 --> 00:13:17.129
A square piece of fish.

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:19.799
Looks a little rough,
right? I like how it tastes.

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:23.702
Filet-O-Fish is better, but
I'd get down on a big fish.

00:13:23.702 --> 00:13:25.337
Remember those chicken
sandwiches from before?

00:13:25.337 --> 00:13:28.340
We got them in wrap form.
Three wraps to choose from.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.642
So, the first one we have is the

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:32.478
classic crispy — ee! Wrap, sorry.

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:34.580
Half a chicken breast.
Half? Come on, guys.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:35.614
Did you really just cut it in half?

00:13:35.614 --> 00:13:37.082
Can't give us the whole one?

00:13:37.082 --> 00:13:40.019
Mayo, lettuce, tomato. Nope.

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:41.253
This one's a spicy one.

00:13:42.621 --> 00:13:43.622
Here's the other half.

00:13:43.622 --> 00:13:44.557
And again, half a chicken wrap.

00:13:44.557 --> 00:13:45.558
I don't know what the price point is,

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:47.426
but you're definitely
getting half of the chicken

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:48.727
you're getting in sandwich form.

00:13:48.727 --> 00:13:50.663
We do have a couple of plant-based options

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:53.265
at our Burger King.
They're not vegan though,

00:13:53.265 --> 00:13:55.901
because they're cooked on the
same grill as the beef burgers

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:57.870
and still contain dairy and eggs.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.906
Just, ah, Burger King, mwah on that one.

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:02.374
The Impossible Whopper,
which we have here.

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:04.577
There's also the single Impossible king.

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:06.178
Couldn't get it for this one.

00:14:06.178 --> 00:14:08.180
"What does the burger taste
like?" you ask, Australia.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.950
Well, first of all, let's
take a look at it. Eeee.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:11.917
Sometimes it looks like beef,

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:14.153
and sometimes, like now, it does not.

00:14:14.153 --> 00:14:16.488
It has mayo on here, and I'm
certain it's not a vegan mayo.

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:18.958
It tastes just like a Whopper.

00:14:18.958 --> 00:14:20.726
Because a Whopper is swimming in mayo,

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.228
and they add something to the meat

00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:24.129
to make it taste like it's char-grilled.

00:14:24.129 --> 00:14:25.831
I mean, I think that everything together,

00:14:25.831 --> 00:14:26.799
because of the toppings and the way

00:14:26.799 --> 00:14:29.068
that they prepare a Whopper

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:31.170
and an Impossible Whopper are the same,

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.972
so I would think, yeah,

00:14:32.972 --> 00:14:34.540
maybe side by side I
could tell a difference,

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.475
but right now this tastes
exactly like a Whopper.

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:38.510
But if we just isolate the meat,

00:14:40.613 --> 00:14:43.182
you can taste a difference
in just the meat, so.

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:44.016
Not my favorite.

00:14:44.016 --> 00:14:45.985
If you're a vegetarian or a vegan,

00:14:45.985 --> 00:14:48.287
well, get it without the mayo.

00:14:48.287 --> 00:14:50.222
If you're not eating meat,

00:14:50.222 --> 00:14:53.859
I would say that the
plant-based Whopper, to me,

00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:55.794
is probably the closest to the real thing

00:14:55.794 --> 00:14:58.297
as far as plant-based
fast-food things are concerned.

00:14:58.297 --> 00:14:59.398
That's my personal opinion.

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:01.834
We actually have two plant-based burgers

00:15:01.834 --> 00:15:03.669
and a fully vegan burger.

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:07.406
The vegan Whopper and
cheese, double vegan patty,

00:15:07.406 --> 00:15:10.109
vegan cheese, vegan mayo,

00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:12.511
and the patty is made from veg.

00:15:12.511 --> 00:15:17.483
We have a plant-based Whopper,
a plant-based Whopper cheese.

00:15:17.483 --> 00:15:21.654
The cheese is not vegan. The
plant-based Angry Whopper.

00:15:21.654 --> 00:15:23.822
Our vegan options are actually vegan,

00:15:23.822 --> 00:15:26.525
as they're cooked separately
from the meat patties,

00:15:26.525 --> 00:15:27.593
which is really good,

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:28.928
because if you're a vegan or a vegetarian

00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:31.263
and you want to come and get a good feed,

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:33.766
then you know it's definitely vegan.

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:35.367
This is the best place to go to.

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:40.139
Yeah, so, "Have a good feed"
in Australian means ...

00:15:40.139 --> 00:15:41.407
how do I even say it? A good feed.

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:44.977
Like, enjoy your meal. If
you want to have a good meal.

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:46.745
If you want to enjoy your meal.

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:50.182
Let's try this vegan Whopper
cheese. Double vegan patty.

00:15:53.118 --> 00:15:54.520
This is a good option.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.423
If you did want an
alternative, I like this.

00:15:57.423 --> 00:15:59.325
And if you just didn't want any meat,

00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:02.061
it's very filling,
there's a lot of flavor.

00:16:02.061 --> 00:16:05.030
It's got a herby taste to it.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.400
You can taste the onion.
The cheese is good too.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.369
I just want to try the cheese separately

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:12.671
just to see if that adds any flavor.

00:16:14.206 --> 00:16:18.610
The cheese is just a bit
creamy. Creamy texture.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.246
A bit more of a smoky flavor,

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:22.715
subtle smoky flavor throughout.

00:16:22.715 --> 00:16:23.549
On to the sides.

00:16:23.549 --> 00:16:26.218
Australia, you don't
have these chicken fries?

00:16:26.218 --> 00:16:28.053
Get a load of this.
Isn't this a great idea?

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:30.189
Looks like a fry, right?
Nah, nah, nah, nah, nah.

00:16:30.189 --> 00:16:32.024
This is a piece of chicken.

00:16:32.024 --> 00:16:33.692
They come in, I don't know
how many different options.

00:16:33.692 --> 00:16:35.761
We got the four-piece,
and it came in a bag.

00:16:35.761 --> 00:16:37.863
It usually comes in a fun
little box, but whatever.

00:16:37.863 --> 00:16:39.198
These things are fantastic.

00:16:39.198 --> 00:16:40.532
Mozzarella sticks,

00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:43.769
come in four and eight pieces.

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:46.138
No way I can do this pull.

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:47.373
These have been sitting for a minute.

00:16:47.373 --> 00:16:48.540
Wait ...

00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:53.946
Yo ... no. Comes with marinara sauce.

00:16:54.913 --> 00:16:56.482
Our BK also has applesauce,

00:16:56.482 --> 00:16:58.417
but they unfortunately forgot it.

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.586
So no sauce.

00:17:00.586 --> 00:17:03.455
And in Australia, these
are our exclusive sides.

00:17:03.455 --> 00:17:07.126
We have a three nuggets
and chip carry cup,

00:17:07.126 --> 00:17:10.129
and we have a pop'n chick'n carry cup

00:17:10.129 --> 00:17:13.432
and a pop'n chick'n carry cup 20-pack.

00:17:13.432 --> 00:17:15.534
However, those were not available.

00:17:15.534 --> 00:17:17.102
But we do have a load of other sauces.

00:17:17.102 --> 00:17:19.872
You know what that means! Sauce talk.

00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:21.306
Sauce talk.

00:17:21.306 --> 00:17:24.009
Now we're going to talk
about all the sauces we have

00:17:24.009 --> 00:17:27.112
that are exclusive to
Australian Hungry Jack's,

00:17:27.112 --> 00:17:30.182
starting with a barbecue plum sauce.

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:34.153
Aioli. And aioli's not just garlic mayo.

00:17:34.153 --> 00:17:37.389
Traditionally it's made
with garlic and olive oil,

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:40.492
whereas mayo uses oil and egg yolks.

00:17:40.492 --> 00:17:43.829
And then we have our spicy sauce.

00:17:43.829 --> 00:17:45.330
How spicy is it?

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.665
I'm about to tell you right now

00:17:46.665 --> 00:17:49.201
because I'm going to crack into this.

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:50.035
Let's go.

00:17:53.172 --> 00:17:54.673
It's not that spicy.

00:17:54.673 --> 00:17:57.509
The kick comes after. It is spicy.

00:17:57.509 --> 00:18:01.113
Barbecue plum. Never heard
of a barbecue plum before.

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:03.782
That's really good!

00:18:03.782 --> 00:18:06.552
It's sweet. It's got that sweet plum,

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:09.121
kind of jam, marmalade flavor,

00:18:09.121 --> 00:18:11.890
but with that barbecue sauce through it.

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:14.526
But I feel like the plum
taste comes through more.

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:15.761
I really like that.

00:18:15.761 --> 00:18:17.896
All right, barbecue.

00:18:20.732 --> 00:18:22.601
Fantastic. Honey mustard.

00:18:25.337 --> 00:18:27.439
It's OK. Here's our ranch.

00:18:27.439 --> 00:18:29.741
America is obsessed with ranch.

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:33.445
I, of course, am not. But I'll try it.

00:18:33.445 --> 00:18:35.314
Yeah, it's fine. All
ranch tastes the same.

00:18:35.314 --> 00:18:37.082
Moving out, we got Buffalo sauce.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:41.019
Pretty good. So, we got
zesty sauce, Australia.

00:18:41.019 --> 00:18:42.688
I don't know if this is
just for dipping stuff

00:18:42.688 --> 00:18:44.022
or if it's on a burger.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.824
I don't think I've heard of this before.

00:18:45.824 --> 00:18:48.193
Maybe we had it before
on other "Food Wars"

00:18:48.193 --> 00:18:49.294
and I just don't remember.

00:18:49.294 --> 00:18:50.996
Let's see how zesty it is.

00:18:50.996 --> 00:18:53.232
Oh, man, that is zesty!

00:18:53.232 --> 00:18:55.667
It's like a strong
mustard, but also creamy.

00:18:56.702 --> 00:18:57.603
And brown mustard.

00:18:57.603 --> 00:18:59.438
Also, we have sweet and sour sauce.

00:18:59.438 --> 00:19:02.508
More for nuggets than it is
for fries, but why not, right?

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:06.278
And before, the marinara, you know I love.

00:19:06.278 --> 00:19:09.181
We have other sauces you
can get here in the US,

00:19:09.181 --> 00:19:12.151
including stacker sauce; mustard and mayo;

00:19:12.151 --> 00:19:15.754
tartar sauce; royal sauce,
King Charles' favorite;

00:19:15.754 --> 00:19:18.023
and a spicy glaze sauce.

00:19:18.023 --> 00:19:21.193
Hungry Jack's also has
some brekkie options.

00:19:21.193 --> 00:19:25.230
Just note, brekkie is short for
breakfast here in Australia.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:28.567
If you're aware, we love
to shorten our words.

00:19:28.567 --> 00:19:31.870
So we will call afternoon arvo.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.908
We'll call a snag for a sausage.

00:19:35.908 --> 00:19:37.509
Tucker is dinner.

00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:39.711
Back to the items here.

00:19:39.711 --> 00:19:43.615
Here we have a bacon and
egg Turkish brekkie roll.

00:19:43.615 --> 00:19:47.286
We have our sausage and
egg Turkish brekkie roll.

00:19:47.286 --> 00:19:49.254
We have our Jack's brekkie roll,

00:19:49.254 --> 00:19:51.690
we have our barbecue brekkie wrap,

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.125
and we have our big brekkie wrap,

00:19:53.125 --> 00:19:54.193
which is the same as that one.

00:19:54.193 --> 00:19:56.028
It just has hash browns in it.

00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:58.063
And then we have pancakes.

00:19:58.063 --> 00:20:00.666
And on to our cheese toasties.

00:20:00.666 --> 00:20:04.002
A cheese toastie. We have
ham and cheese toasties

00:20:04.002 --> 00:20:07.673
and a ham, cheese, and tomato toastie.

00:20:07.673 --> 00:20:10.342
US, we love our fast-food breakfast,

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:13.278
or brekkie, as you call it in Australia.

00:20:13.278 --> 00:20:16.215
Starting down here, we
have French toast sticks.

00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:17.316
Frekkies, I guess.

00:20:17.316 --> 00:20:18.717
You can get them in three or five.

00:20:18.717 --> 00:20:21.453
Has this nice little syrupy dipping sauce.

00:20:21.453 --> 00:20:22.387
That's just OK.

00:20:22.387 --> 00:20:24.856
We have a lot of breakfast
sandwiches in the US.

00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:28.527
You can get a breakfast sandwich
in different bread forms.

00:20:28.527 --> 00:20:30.462
The first one we have is a biscuit.

00:20:30.462 --> 00:20:33.031
Don't know if you have these in Australia.

00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:34.566
Try to explain it to non-Americans

00:20:34.566 --> 00:20:37.502
what American biscuits are,
easier just to show you.

00:20:37.502 --> 00:20:38.937
You have KFC, right?

00:20:38.937 --> 00:20:41.039
It's like those biscuits you get at KFC.

00:20:41.039 --> 00:20:43.075
We have these breakfast
sandwiches. See this little thing?

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:45.077
It's, like, the driest thing in the world,

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:46.712
but we have breakfast sandwiches.

00:20:46.712 --> 00:20:48.714
Here's a bacon, egg, and cheese one.

00:20:48.714 --> 00:20:50.816
You can also get sausage, egg, and cheese;

00:20:50.816 --> 00:20:51.750
ham, egg, and cheese.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.485
Good, dry. I really don't go for those,

00:20:53.485 --> 00:20:56.088
but what I do like are
the Croissan'wiches,

00:20:56.088 --> 00:20:59.024
another bread option
where it is a croissant.

00:20:59.024 --> 00:21:01.293
Yes, a croissant, France.

00:21:01.293 --> 00:21:04.496
And we stuck a bunch of meat
and cheese inside of it.

00:21:04.496 --> 00:21:08.667
Going to go with the,
this one is the bacon one.

00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:10.769
A fully loaded, oh, God.

00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:15.741
Sausage and ham and bacon.

00:21:15.741 --> 00:21:17.609
Oh, my goodness.

00:21:17.609 --> 00:21:22.180
Every version of pork in one sandwich

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.248
with eggs.

00:21:23.248 --> 00:21:24.449
I have to know.

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:31.690
Kind of wish I didn't.
Kind of wish I didn't. Ugh.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:33.692
Biscuits or croissants. These
are the ones you can get.

00:21:33.692 --> 00:21:35.160
I'm going to throw
on-screen the whole list

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.362
of both the options that you have.

00:21:37.362 --> 00:21:38.730
I can't list them all.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.365
It's just a different version of the bread

00:21:40.365 --> 00:21:42.901
with a meat, an egg, and a cheese.

00:21:42.901 --> 00:21:46.538
Also they have breakfast
burritos. Believe it.

00:21:46.538 --> 00:21:49.608
This one, whoo, yo, dog.
This is a hefty boy.

00:21:49.608 --> 00:21:54.513
This I believe is the
Egg-Normous Burrito. Come on.

00:21:54.513 --> 00:21:55.981
This thing is, like,

00:21:55.981 --> 00:21:58.183
this has gotta be, this is
like a Chipotle burrito.

00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.985
Look at the size of this thing, Yuelei!

00:21:59.985 --> 00:22:01.286
See what's inside.

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:06.325
Australia, I assure
you this is not normal.

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:09.828
Hash browns, bacon, sausage,

00:22:09.828 --> 00:22:12.130
an egg, cheese.

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:13.765
And also comes with

00:22:15.067 --> 00:22:18.904
a picante salsa, which, we will
find out together how it is.

00:22:21.873 --> 00:22:24.009
Breakfast burritos are
a big thing in America,

00:22:24.009 --> 00:22:24.943
probably in the UK as well,

00:22:24.943 --> 00:22:27.813
but this is just ridiculous.

00:22:27.813 --> 00:22:28.680
It's actually really good.

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:30.816
And you know what?
Secret weapon, the salsa.

00:22:30.816 --> 00:22:34.219
I don't know who makes
the salsa, but yeah, dude.

00:22:34.219 --> 00:22:37.489
I'm having a comeback right now. Mm!

00:22:37.489 --> 00:22:41.026
If you want a breakfast
burrito in not-gigantic form,

00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:42.961
there's also a breakfast burrito Jr.

00:22:42.961 --> 00:22:44.129
Got yourself a sweet tooth?

00:22:44.129 --> 00:22:46.365
We have two exclusive desserts in the US.

00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:48.767
Right here, two chocolate chip cookies.

00:22:48.767 --> 00:22:52.471
Also, we have this Hershey's sundae pie.

00:22:52.471 --> 00:22:53.872
Sundae pie on the go.

00:22:53.872 --> 00:22:55.574
Look at this thing. Look at this thing!

00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:56.475
You see that, Yuelei?

00:22:57.843 --> 00:22:59.444
I'm kind of mad now
that I know this exists.

00:22:59.444 --> 00:23:00.612
I'm going to want it all the time.

00:23:00.612 --> 00:23:04.216
And at Hungry Jack's, these
are our dessert options.

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:07.386
We have a Storm Biscoff,
which wasn't available;

00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:10.789
a Storm bubblegum; a Storm Oreo;

00:23:10.789 --> 00:23:13.258
a Storm Cadbury Flake;

00:23:13.258 --> 00:23:17.162
a Storm M&amp;M's mini; a sticky date pudding;

00:23:17.162 --> 00:23:20.332
a caramel sundae; a strawberry sundae;

00:23:20.332 --> 00:23:24.403
a chocolate sundae; and a
mini Drumstick, vanilla.

00:23:24.403 --> 00:23:26.538
Storms, if you're not too familiar,

00:23:26.538 --> 00:23:29.341
I would say it's quite
similar to a McFlurry.

00:23:29.341 --> 00:23:31.610
The bubblegum looks a
little bit terrifying.

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:32.844
I really want to try it.

00:23:32.844 --> 00:23:34.713
It looks kind of gross.

00:23:34.713 --> 00:23:38.250
With the marshmallows on top,
it looks ridiculously sweet.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:42.421
This is all that I had
to try my ice cream with.

00:23:45.891 --> 00:23:50.796
That was so sweet. It
was putrid. It was foul.

00:23:50.796 --> 00:23:52.764
I don't even think a
child would like that.

00:23:52.764 --> 00:23:54.933
That is ... uh-uh.

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:57.035
You can't go wrong with an
Oreo. I always get them.

00:23:57.035 --> 00:23:58.503
But a Flake will be good.

00:23:58.503 --> 00:24:00.739
The chocolate is a bit shredded.

00:24:03.542 --> 00:24:07.479
That is a bit of me. That
is a bit of me! Mm-hmm.

00:24:07.479 --> 00:24:11.716
Nice, creamy, and then a delicious taste

00:24:11.716 --> 00:24:14.619
of flaky milk chocolate.

00:24:14.619 --> 00:24:17.789
Burst of flavor in your
mouth, not overpowering,

00:24:17.789 --> 00:24:19.357
and not feeling like you're
going to have to end up

00:24:19.357 --> 00:24:21.193
